  "notes": "VERB TYPE:\n{他動詞|たどうし} (transitive verb)\nGodan verb ({五段動詞|ごだんどうし})\n\n・{賜|たまわ}らない (negative)\n・{賜|たまわ}って (te-form)\n・{賜|たまわ}った (past)\n\nREGISTER:\nVery formal/honorific. Used in business correspondence, formal speeches, and when addressing royalty or high-status individuals.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n・ご{意見|いけん}を{賜|たまわ}る - to receive your opinion\n・ご{指導|しどう}を{賜|たまわ}る - to receive guidance\n・お{時間|じかん}を{賜|たまわ}る - to receive your time\n\nRELATED KEIGO:\n・{賜|たま}う - archaic form (used in classical Japanese)\n・{頂|いただ}く - less formal humble form of receiving",
